Grading the pasted ASHFALL OUTPOST HTML directly from source — this is a read-only analysis task (grading a single pasted file, no repo, nothing to implement), so I'm answering directly rather than treating it as a plan-mode coding task.

## Worksheet

**F1 Core loop** — GameState holds all state; `PRNG` (Mulberry32) used via `this.prng`, no `Math.random` found; `endTurn()` calls produce→consume→updateColonists→storm→events in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 Map** — `generateMap()` builds 64 tiles from `prng.next()`; `canBuild()` checks `req.terrain.includes(tile.terrain)`; `getAdjacencyBonus()` multiplies into `output` in `produceResources()`. Score 2.

**F3 Economy** — greenhouse consumes water→food, forge consumes power→metal; caps enforced via `Math.min(..., resourceCaps[k])`. Score 2.

**F4 Population** — colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job; `avgSkill`/`avgMorale` read in `produceResources()`, but `fatigue` is never read by production, only indirectly nudges morale later. Score 1.

**F5 Needs** — `consumeResources()` docks morale on shortage; `avgMorale` feeds `produceResources()`; morale recovers +2/turn when resting. Score 2.

**F6 Research** — 8 nodes, prereqs enforced, costs deducted, but only `efficiency` and `storm_defense` actually alter behavior; `vent_tech`, `water_purify`, `population`, `advanced_farm`, `power_plant`, `final_tech` are never read anywhere. Score 1.

**F7 Events** — 10 entries in `eventDetails`; selection is `prng.choice(eventList)` — plain uniform, not weighted (unused `weights` var exists only for terrain); cooldowns via `eventCooldowns`; 6+ events have real divergent-effect choices. Score 1.

**F8 Trade** — `generateTradePrices()` is base+random noise regenerated per caravan, never reads `resources`; displayed "stock" is cosmetic and not enforced as a buy limit. Score 1.

**F9 Hazard** — `ashStorm()` fires every 15 turns, severity scales with turn, `storm_defense` cuts damage 30%; but `produceResources()` never reads `building.hp`, and nothing in code ever restores `hp` (repair text in `dust_storm` event only spends parts, touches no building). Score 1.

**F10 Save/load** — `serialize()`/`deserialize()` round-trip via JSON textarea; `confirmLoad()` alerts "Invalid save data" on parse failure. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions** — `checkEndConditions()` has reachable win (turn≥60, pop≥12, needs met) and lose (pop=0); `showEndScreen()` sums population/research/resources/turn score. Score 2.

**F12 UI** — `switchTab()` wired to tab buttons; log entries show `[T${entry.turn}]`; `showTooltip()` on map tiles; keydown handles Space + digit tab shortcuts; `@media (max-width:600px)` reflows layout. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel** — `runTests()` has 15 real invariant checks (caps, ranges, prereqs, save/load hash match); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 turns headless on a fresh `GameState`, prints `getHash()`. Score 2.

**G1 research→yield** — `research.efficiency.done` read in `produceResources()`, but the line does `const output = ...; output *= 1.2;` — reassigning a `const` throws a TypeError at runtime, so the multiplier never actually applies once triggered. Score 1.

**G2 shortfall→morale→output** — `consumeResources()` docks morale on shortage; `produceResources()` (next turn) reads `avgMorale` into `baseOutput`; real one-turn-lag pipeline, fixed-magnitude penalty. Score 3.

**G3 storm→damage→output→repair** — `ashStorm()` sets `building.hp` down, but `produceResources()` never checks `hp`, and no code path ever restores `hp` — damaged buildings produce at full rate forever. Score 1.

**G4 trade prices vs stockpile/supply** — `generateTradePrices()` = fixed base + fresh random noise per caravan cycle; never reads `this.resources` or any persisting drift variable. Score 0.

**G5 event choices mutate state** — `new_settler`'s "Recruit" pushes a durable colonist and spends scrip; `dust_storm`'s two branches durably spend parts vs. drop morale array-wide; effects go straight into `gs.resources`/`gs.colonists`. Score 4.

